message: "If you use this repository, cite it and the paper it studies."
title: "Subexponential ECDL: a claim-by-claim research hillclimb"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arun
    given-names: Rohan
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rohanarun/subexponential-ecdl-hillclimb"
abstract: >
  An auto-research harness for the conditional subexponential ECDL paper. The
  repository separates the paper's reduction from the unverified external
  theorem it depends on, and gates claim statuses on committed evidence.
keywords:
  - elliptic curve discrete logarithm
  - boolean tensor network
  - index calculus
  - formal verification
  - research automation
